From 07cc93c29b80f3645601cdb3130ccdd86d293180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:12:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Air battle sound, release 2, second part: strikes, close
 flak, big moments, dead engines, the battle's music

- Rounds striking a plane heard near the camera (mix.json air.roundsHit; the ridden plane's own at the camera). The
  mix lists no takes yet: silent until Brian marks round seven's hits, then no code change.
- A flak burst within 100 m of the camera plays grenade_blast in every view (air.closeView.closeFlak).
- Big moments (mix.json big, air.bigDuck): a plane going down near the camera, a burst within 20 m, a stick within
  120 m plays at full while the bed, loops, close takes and music dip by big.duckDb (attack, hold, release).
- Dead engines thin the drones (air.engineLost): the ridden plane's own, and each formation's by the engines still
  turning against the most it flew with.
- The air battle's meter eases by intensity.rise and fall instead of a per-frame step.
- The battle's music (mix.json music): Zero Hour from the start, crossfading into The Advance or Trench Line At
  Twilight at first contact at -8 dB, down to -18 in the thick of it, back in a lull, up at the swing; at the end
  the battle's sounds come down 10 dB and The Field Is Ours or The Line Gives Way plays. ACampaignGameMode gains a
  battle score (Begin, Contact, Level, End, Stop) that holds the map's moods while a battle scene runs.
- Sounds/Real: grenade_blast, with credits. mix.json v5 (no number changes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz35oCkUv94Xb2EwCjp
